In article <984@madnix.UUCP> jeffm@madnix.UUCP (Jeff Metzner) writes:
>Some questions and comments about the Mac port of Nethack 3.0, patchlevel 6:
>
>(1)  Has anyone successfully compiled lev_comp with THINK C 4?  I keep getting
>     "data segment too big" errors.

Yes. Me. Check that separate STRs is selected in the Project Type dialogue
box. Make sure that you've read the Install.mac file. The changes for
pl6 to the lev files were not propagated to lev_comp.c and lev_lex.c.
Make sure that the changes are in these files. This should give you about
200 bytes free. Then you're kosher.

>(2)  Do I even need to compile lev_comp?  Will the compiled levels from my 
>     office Unix system work if I transfer them to my Mac?

No, you don't have to use the special level compiler on a Mac. I'm one of
the first to do it on a Mac. Several others have done what you suggested.
Remember to do a binary transfer of the files over to the Mac.

>
>(3)  Invisiblity doesn't work right.  The cursor disappears, and the position
>     of the invisible character can't be seen.

It was designed that way. To me invisible means invisible (but with
the changes I plan to make for pl7, that won't be exactly true anymore).
If enough people complain, this "feature" can change.

>(4)  How do I set NETHACKOPTIONS so that I don't have to enter my name and
>     my pet's name every game?
In the pl6 Mac port, you can't. I have the code for an options dialogue box
for pl7.

